[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Requirements Specification - Component ODE Models
UID: DOC-SSS002
VERSION: 1.1.0
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SSS2-ELECTRODES
TITLE: Iron electrode, hydrogen evolution, and dual air electrodes

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Each DynamicComponent in this document is the software image of a patented plant
part. Iron, ORR, OER, electrolyte, separator, collector, cell, stack, module,
and enclosure geometries are taken from US12308414B2 (Claims 1-18 and FIGS. 1-93)
and EP4602674A1 (Claims 1-89 and FIGS. 1-27). Balance-of-plant electrical and
thermal components remain required to close the LODES plant of US12308414B2
FIGS. 94-102.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FE-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Iron electrode ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module plant_sim.components.iron_anode SHALL provide class IronAnode
(notebook plant_sim/01_IronAnode.ipynb).

The component SHALL dynamically model metallic iron, Fe(OH)2, Fe3O4, active surface
area, passivation thickness, porosity, electrode temperature, and irreversible
active-material loss.

The RHS SHALL calculate iron phase derivatives from the shared reaction network.

The iron electrode SHALL support DRI pellet beds (US12308414B2 Claim 18), porous
particle assemblies, and channeled rib-and-spine electrodes (EP4602674A1 Claim 1)
with areal loading 1-7 g Fe/cm2 and electrolyte volume fraction 0.5-0.9 when
fully charged (EP4602674A1 Claim 16-17).

Channel length, width, spacing, shape, slope, channel fraction, and spine/rib
porosity SHALL match IA-SYS-016 and IA-SYS-018. Position relative to ORR and OER
SHALL be changeable (US12308414B2 Claim 13).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claim 18 and FIG. 3 packed DRI bed; EP4602674A1 Claims 1, 16-17 and
[0051]-[0061]. Thick electrodes need channels to keep HER from dominating charge.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Discharge of Fe increases Fe(OH)2 using IA-CHM-002 stoichiometry. Temperature is a
dynamic state. Passivation thickness is nonnegative.

Changed because ironair.components.iron_electrode / IronElectrode does not exist
(src/ironair/components is an empty package). plant_sim.components.iron_anode.IronAnode
implements the Fe/Fe(OH)2/Fe3O4 Faraday ODE used by the plant stack.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-HER-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Hydrogen evolution ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.hydrogen SHALL provide class HydrogenEvolution.

States SHALL include hydrogen inventory and applicable interfacial or gas-transfer dynamics.

The component SHALL couple hydrogen generation to charging current and electrode potential.

Vertical channels SHALL provide a bubble-egress path for HER (EP4602674A1 [0056]).
Coulombic efficiency SHALL decrease when ionic path length to the back of a thick
iron electrode exceeds the resistance of front-surface HER (EP4602674A1 [0047]).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 [0044]-[0047], [0056]. Enclosure ventilation and lid venting in
US12308414B2 remove evolved hydrogen from the vessel headspace.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
H2 inventory increases under negative iron overpotential. Open-circuit HER is smaller
than strong cathodic charging HER.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-ORR-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oxygen reduction ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.oxygen_reduction SHALL provide class OxygenReduction.

States SHALL include interfacial charge storage and oxygen availability where applicable.

The component SHALL calculate nonlinear ORR kinetics and oxygen consumption.

ORR SHALL be configurable as floating, vertical natural-air-breathing, inverse
air-breathing, tubular, stacked submerged sections with depth-equalized pressure
drop, wavy/rippled, or bifunctional, per IA-SYS-009 and IA-SYS-012
(US12308414B2 Claims 1, 4, 7-12).

One ORR face SHALL face electrolyte or channels and the opposing face SHALL
contact air (EP4602674A1 Claim 1). Hydrophobic GDE layers with PTFE/carbon MPL
examples from US12308414B2 SHALL be parameterizable.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 1, 4, 7-12 and cathode construction; EP4602674A1 Claim 1
air-facing second surface.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
ORR current is negative (cathodic) for eta < 0 versus the ORR Nernst potential.
Oxygen consumption matches Faraday's law for four-electron ORR.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-OER-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oxygen evolution ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.oxygen_evolution SHALL provide class OxygenEvolution.

The component SHALL calculate oxygen evolution, catalyst activity, and applicable
dynamic electrode states.

OER SHALL support planar, submerged, interdigitated trunk-and-projection,
corrugated, serpentine, discrete cathode arrays, spiral bifilar, and pleated
layouts (EP4602674A1 Claims 1, 3, 12, 32, 38, 70, 77).

Default OER construction SHALL be porous metal mesh plus oxygen-evolution
catalyst (Claim 11). OER SHALL sit closer to the iron electrode than ORR during
charge and SHALL be electrically isolatable from ORR (US12308414B2 FIGS. 5A-5B).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 Claims 1, 3, 11-12, 38, 70, 77; US12308414B2 dual-cathode toggle.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
OER current is positive (anodic) for eta > 0 versus the OER Nernst potential.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-GDL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Gas diffusion ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.gas_diffusion SHALL provide class GasDiffusionLayer.

The component SHALL calculate transient oxygen concentration profiles, effective
diffusion, pore saturation, flooding, and gas/liquid transport.

Hydraulic head on vertical ORR SHALL be able to drive liquid migration and
flooding; OER bubbles trapped at a horizontal air electrode SHALL be able to
dry the triple-phase boundary (US12308414B2 vertical versus horizontal
architecture discussion, FIGS. 8-9B). Stacked submerged ORR SHALL capture
cascading bubbles with baffles, lips, or increasing pocket thickness
(FIGS. 25A-36B, Claims 1 and 14-15).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 flooding, dry-out, bubble-trap, and stacked-core air utilization.
pO2 window 0.01-100 atm discharge and 0.001-100 atm charge.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
A step decrease in boundary O2 mole fraction produces a delayed interior O2 decline.
Flooding (saturation -> 1) reduces effective O2 diffusivity.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-ELY-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrolyte ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.electrolyte SHALL provide class Electrolyte.

States SHALL include water inventory, dissolved species, electrolyte temperature,
carbonation, and spatial concentration distributions where enabled.

The model SHALL include concentration-dependent KOH physical properties.

Default composition SHALL be 6 M aqueous KOH. Alternate patented mixtures from
IA-SYS-021 SHALL be selectable. Carbonation from CO2-bearing air SHALL consume
OH- and MAY precipitate solids that clog pores (US12308414B2). High hydroxide
(7 M or greater) SHALL be allowed as a capacity and coulombic-efficiency lever
(EP4602674A1).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 electrolyte examples and CO2 discussion; EP4602674A1 Claims 14-15
and high-hydroxide paragraph.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Conductivity is computed from instantaneous KOH concentration and temperature via
ironair.properties. Carbonate accumulation consumes OH-.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SEP-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Separator ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.separator SHALL provide class Separator.

The model SHALL represent transient species transport, electrolyte saturation where
applicable, degradation, and separator temperature.

Ionic resistance SHALL be calculated from the instantaneous physical state.

The separator SHALL be able to block dissolved oxygen and oxygen bubbles from
reaching the iron electrode without a substantial ionic-resistance penalty, while
remaining hydrophilic and macroporous (US12308414B2 FIG. 4A). It MAY be a
compression frame, porous insulator, ribbed bubble-egress structure, or porous
dielectric coating on iron and/or OER (EP4602674A1 [0048], Claim 2). Wrapped
stacked-core separators MAY use 1 micrometer to 1 centimeter pores
(US12308414B2 FIG. 36A).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 oxygen-blocking separator; EP4602674A1 Claim 2 and [0048].
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
R_ionic is algebraic in conductivity, thickness, area, and saturation. Temperature
is dynamic.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-COL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Current collector ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.current_collector SHALL provide class CurrentCollector.

The model SHALL include thermal dynamics and configurable long-term contact or
resistance degradation.

Ohmic voltage loss SHALL be calculated algebraically.

Collectors SHALL include anode branch-plus-primary layouts, ORR dual-face tabs,
Ni-coated-steel ORR collectors with EPDM gasket compression
(US12308414B2 FIGS. 4B-4C), stainless-steel wires/sheets or mesh cages in iron
ribs (EP4602674A1), and can-negative housings (US12308414B2 Claim 5).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 5 and 17 and FIGS. 4B-4C; EP4602674A1 Claims 13, 30-31.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No fake lag state for resistance. V_ohm = I * R(T, degradation_state).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-CEL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Complete cell ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.cell SHALL provide class IronAirCell.

The cell SHALL couple iron electrode, air electrode, hydrogen evolution, electrolyte,
separator, gas diffusion, current collectors, and thermal dynamics.

The cell SHALL calculate instantaneous terminal voltage, current, power, SOC, and
available capacity.

The component SHALL solve coupled nonlinear electrochemical and electrical constraints.

Charge SHALL close iron to OER to power source; discharge SHALL close iron to ORR
to load (EP4602674A1 [0049]). Independent charge and discharge length scales
SHALL be parameterizable (US12308414B2 Lc versus Ld, including 100 h / 300 h
asymmetric example). Shared-electrolyte baths of multiple cells SHALL be allowed
(US12308414B2 FIG. 9A vessel 970).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 dual-electrode switch; US12308414B2 dual-cathode and duration scaling.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Cell rhs solves algebraic current/voltage consistency. Outputs include V, I, P, SOC.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-008

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SSS2-BOP
TITLE: Thermal, air, and electrolyte hydraulic plant

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-THM-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Thermal ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.thermal SHALL provide class ThermalNetwork.

States SHALL include thermal energy or temperature at relevant physical nodes.

The model SHALL calculate conduction, convection, radiation, reaction heat, and cooling.

Vessel cavity flow (air or liquid), thermal-mass water fill, and lid-level thermal
management from US12308414B2 FIGS. 1E-1F and 9A SHALL map onto ThermalNetwork
nodes. Wide/low vessels SHALL be usable to increase surface area for heat
rejection.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 double-wall cavity 161 and multi-function lid thermal management.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Adiabatic isolated node with positive heat source increases temperature.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-AIR-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Air handling ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.air_system SHALL provide class AirSystem.

The component SHALL include gas inventories, manifold pressure dynamics, oxygen
concentration, humidity, and airflow coupling.

Air delivery SHALL include natural air-breathing, forced supply, sparging/bubbling
into submerged ORR, cascading stacked-core flow, snorkel/test-tube mixed-phase
channels, and ramp arrays with holes (US12308414B2 Claims 9, 14-15; FIGS. 37-51,
71A-71B). Outlet pressure regulation SHALL be able to hold unsealed air-chamber
pressure.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 air-supply and stacked-core architectures. Equal pressure drop across
depth-stacked ORR sections is Claim 1.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Manifold pressure rises when inlet mass flow exceeds outlet plus consumption.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-AIR-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fan ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.fan SHALL provide class Fan.

The model SHALL include rotor speed dynamics and fan power consumption.

Fan/blower air SHALL be able to feed submerged ORR stacks and lid air-distribution
plenums of US12308414B2 FIG. 9A.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Rotor speed is a dynamic state. Electrical power is an algebraic output from speed and torque.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-AIR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FLD-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrolyte circulation ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.electrolyte_flow SHALL provide class ElectrolyteFlow.

The component SHALL dynamically track flow, species transfer, pressure or hydraulic
storage where physically justified, and temperature.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Species transport delay appears when using the detailed hydraulic mode.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FLD-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pump ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.pump SHALL provide class Pump.

The component SHALL model motor and hydraulic response, electrical input, and mechanical losses.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Shaft speed is dynamic. Hydraulic power is less than electrical input by documented efficiency.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FLD-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reservoir ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.reservoir SHALL provide class Reservoir.

The component SHALL model liquid inventory, chemical species inventories, temperature,
and boundary flows.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Mass balance: dM/dt equals inlet minus outlet minus leak.
The vessel cavity MAY hold drained electrolyte during maintenance
(US12308414B2 FIGS. 1E-1F) without requiring off-site storage volume.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FLD-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Valve ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.valve SHALL provide class Valve.

The component SHALL model actuator response, valve position, and flow-dependent
hydraulic characteristics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Position is a dynamic actuator state. Flow is algebraic in position and pressure drop.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FLD-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Piping ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.piping SHALL provide class Pipe.

The component SHALL model transient fluid transport and temperature or species
residence-time dynamics when using the detailed hydraulic mode.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Detailed mode has at least one transport delay state. Lumped mode is flagged reduced_order.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-HEX-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Heat exchanger ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.heat_exchanger SHALL provide class HeatExchanger.

The component SHALL represent thermal storage and dynamic heat transfer between fluid circuits.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Two fluid temperatures approach each other under heat transfer with no external loss.
Cavity coolant and lid thermal loops of US12308414B2 SHALL be representable as
HeatExchanger circuits.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SSS2-PLANT
TITLE: Stack, module, enclosure, and electrical conversion

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-STK-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stack ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.stack SHALL provide class BatteryStack.

The component SHALL aggregate cell states while preserving cell-level variations and
electrical current conservation.

Stacked vessels with conductive contact points SHALL be able to place cells in
series (US12308414B2 Claim 3). Arrays of coaxial ORR-core / hexagonal-anode cells
in a shared electrolyte pool (FIGS. 27-34) and multi-cell housings with dividing
walls (FIG. 13) SHALL be supported. Double-sided and air-channel-paired cells
from EP4602674A1 Claims 18-19 SHALL be stackable.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 3 and 5, FIGS. 13 and 27-34; EP4602674A1 Claims 18-19.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Series stack current is identical through cells. Terminal voltage is the sum of cell voltages.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-MOD-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Module ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.module SHALL provide class BatteryModule.

The model SHALL include coupled stacks, shared fluid equipment, air equipment, and thermal states.

A module MAY be a stack of 40 housings as illustrated in US12308414B2 FIG. 13,
sharing lid air distribution, venting, and DC connections (FIG. 9A).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Module assembles at least one stack plus shared thermal or fluid nodes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-ENC-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Enclosure ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.enclosure SHALL provide class BatteryEnclosure.

The model SHALL include enclosure temperature, ventilation, auxiliary electrical loads,
and enclosure-level gas inventories.

The enclosure SHALL implement stackable-vessel, double-wall secondary containment,
optional bag-in-box, trough/dished mechanical shapes, and multi-function lid
(air distribution, process-gas vent, thermal management, current collection,
controls/sensing, DC connections) from US12308414B2 Claims 3 and 5 and
FIGS. 1E-1F, 9A, 12A-12F. Alkaline electrolyte SHALL have primary plus secondary
containment.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claim 3 vessel, Claim 5 can-negative housing, hazardous-electrolyte
containment, and lid 902 functions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Ventilation flow reduces enclosure H2 inventory. Auxiliary load is an algebraic electrical output.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-DC-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DC bus ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.dc_bus SHALL provide class DCBus.

The component SHALL model DC link capacitor voltage and stored energy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
C * V * dV/dt equals net electrical power into the capacitor.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-CNV-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DC/DC converter ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.dc_converter SHALL provide class DCDCConverter.

The model SHALL include averaged inductor current, capacitor voltage, and converter losses.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Averaged inductor current is a dynamic state. Losses increase output current demand.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-INV-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Inverter ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.inverter SHALL provide class GridInverter.

The model SHALL include averaged electrical control dynamics, DC link interaction,
and active/reactive power response.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
P and Q track references through explicit controller states, not prescribed algebraic jumps only.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-TRF-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Transformer ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.transformer SHALL provide class Transformer.

The component SHALL include electromagnetic dynamic states where detailed transient
modeling is enabled, along with winding and core thermal dynamics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Detailed mode includes flux or current states. Thermal states exist in both modes.
Prescribed grid voltage is an input, not a transformer state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-GRD-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Grid interface ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.grid SHALL provide class GridInterface.

The grid SHALL support dynamic voltage and frequency disturbances, network interface
equations, and configurable external-grid dynamic models.

A prescribed grid voltage or frequency SHALL be treated as an external input, not an
invented dynamic state.

Grid-connected LODES dispatch of surplus solar over seasonal windows
(US12308414B2 Definitions; FIGS. 94-102 bulk energy storage systems) SHALL be
representable as GridInterface scenarios.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
When voltage/frequency are prescribed, they appear in inputs. Optional swing-equation
mode is explicitly identified.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-DEG-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Degradation ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.degradation SHALL provide class Degradation.

The model SHALL represent irreversible material changes, catalyst decay, resistance
growth, and active capacity loss.

ORR damage from high OER potential, PTFE hydrophobicity loss, carbonate pore
clogging, salt crusting on air electrodes, and iron passivation SHALL be
representable aging modes (US12308414B2 dual-cathode isolation, CO2, and crusting
discussion; EP4602674A1 passivation via Fe(OH)2 films). Seasonal anode replacement
SHALL be an allowed discrete maintenance event (US12308414B2 replaceable electrodes).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Degradation states are nondecreasing under positive aging rates. Capacity loss is irreversible.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-FLT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sensor ODE
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.components.sensors SHALL provide class DynamicSensor.

The model SHALL include finite response time, sensor drift, bias, and noise.

Lid-mounted reactor controls and sensing of US12308414B2 FIG. 9A SHALL map onto
DynamicSensor instances for voltage, current, temperature, electrolyte level, gas
flow, and hydrogen.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
First-order sensor lag is a dynamic state. Noise uses a documented random seed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-CTL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Supervisory control dynamics
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.controls.supervisory SHALL provide class SupervisoryController.

The controller SHALL include explicit continuous controller states where applicable,
as well as discrete operating modes.

It SHALL be implemented as a hybrid system with ODE dynamics and discrete transitions.

Discrete modes SHALL include charge (iron-OER-source), discharge (iron-ORR-load),
rest, protection, and optional airflow-flex isolation of ORR from OER
(EP4602674A1 switch 116; US12308414B2 switch 550 and Claim 16).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Mode transitions are event-driven. PI or equivalent continuous states exist for current/power regulation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-EST-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: State estimation
STATEMENT: >>>
Module ironair.controls.estimation SHALL provide class BatteryStateEstimator.

The model SHALL estimate SOC, SOH, active iron inventory, and available charge/discharge power.

It SHALL not access the simulated plant's true hidden states during observer execution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Estimator rhs and update methods accept only measurements and previous estimates,
never plant.y hidden components.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
